IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-joinder`

-- ccc22-tests-joinder.l4 -- tests for ccc22-joinder.l4 (sections 589 to 596). Expected values are written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Section 589`

-- args: the count charges an indictable offence other than murder and is to be joined to a murder count, same transaction, the accused consents.
#ASSERT `s 589 the section bars joining the count to a count that charges murder` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 589 the section bars joining the count to a count that charges murder` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 589 the section bars joining the count to a count that charges murder` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 589 the section bars joining the count to a count that charges murder` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 590`

#ASSERT `s 590(1) the ground alone makes the count objectionable` `s 590(1)(a) it charges in the alternative several different matters, acts or omissions that are stated in the alternative in an enactment that describes as an indictable offence the matters, acts or omissions charged in the count` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 590(1) the ground alone makes the count objectionable` `s 590(1)(b) it is double or multifarious` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 590(1) the ground alone makes the count objectionable` `s 590(1) some other ground` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): args: at a stage of the trial, the count is of kind (a) or (b), the ground is that it embarrasses the accused in their defence.
#ASSERT `s 590(2) the accused may apply to the court to amend or to divide the count` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 590(2) the accused may apply to the court to amend or to divide the count` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 590(2) the accused may apply to the court to amend or to divide the count` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 590(2) the accused may apply to the court to amend or to divide the count` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 590(3) the court may order that the count be amended or divided into two or more counts` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 590(3) the court may order that the count be amended or divided into two or more counts` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where it is satisfied that the ends of justice require it" (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 590(3) a formal commencement may be inserted before each of the counts into which it is divided` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 590(3) a formal commencement may be inserted before each of the counts into which it is divided` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 591`

#ASSERT `s 591(1) any number of counts for any number of offences may be joined in the same indictment, subject to section 589` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 591(1) any number of counts for any number of offences may be joined in the same indictment, subject to section 589` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(1) any number of counts for any number of offences may be joined in the same indictment, subject to section 589` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(1) the counts are distinguished as the subsection requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(1) the counts are distinguished as the subsection requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 591(2) each count may be treated as a separate indictment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(2) each count may be treated as a separate indictment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): args: the court is satisfied that the interests of justice so require, there is more than one accused, the order sought.
#ASSERT `s 591(3) the court may order that the accused or counts be tried separately` TRUE FALSE `s 591(3)(a) that the accused or defendant be tried separately on one or more of the counts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(3) the court may order that the accused or counts be tried separately` TRUE TRUE `s 591(3)(b) that one or more of several accused or defendants be tried separately on one or more of the counts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(3) the court may order that the accused or counts be tried separately` TRUE FALSE `s 591(3)(b) that one or more of several accused or defendants be tried separately on one or more of the counts` EQUALS NOTHING   -- one accused only
#ASSERT `s 591(3) the court may order that the accused or counts be tried separately` FALSE TRUE `s 591(3)(a) that the accused or defendant be tried separately on one or more of the counts` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where it is satisfied that the interests of justice so require"
#ASSERT `s 591(3) the court may order that the accused or counts be tried separately` TRUE TRUE `s 591(3) some other order` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 591(4) an order under subsection (3) may be made` `s 591(4) before the trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(4) an order under subsection (3) may be made` `s 591(4) during the trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(4) an order under subsection (3) may be made` `s 591(4) after the trial` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 591(4) an order under subsection (3) may be made` `s 591(4) after the trial` EQUALS NOTHING`; a period the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05), so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, listed in the fork register as [F:may-where] with the other reading NOTHING
-- (4), the jury: args: the order is made during the trial, the counts are (a) or (b).
#ASSERT `s 591(4) the jury is discharged from giving a verdict on the counts` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(4) the jury is discharged from giving a verdict on the counts` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 591(4) the jury is discharged from giving a verdict on the counts` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4.1): args: takes effect later, the court is satisfied that it is in the interests of justice.
#ASSERT `s 591(4.1) the court may make an order under subsection (3) that takes effect later` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(4.1) the court may make an order under subsection (3) that takes effect later` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 591(4.1) the court may make an order under subsection (3) that takes effect later` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4.2): args: the decisions relate to disclosure, admissibility or the Charter, made (or could have been made) before the evidence on the merits, the court is satisfied it would not be in the interests of justice.
#ASSERT `s 591(4.2) the decisions made before the order takes effect continue to bind the parties` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(4.2) the decisions made before the order takes effect continue to bind the parties` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Unless the court is satisfied"
#ASSERT `s 591(4.2) the decisions made before the order takes effect continue to bind the parties` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- made after the evidence on the merits is presented
#ASSERT `s 591(4.2) the decisions made before the order takes effect continue to bind the parties` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a decision of that kind
#ASSERT `s 591(5) the counts may subsequently be proceeded on as if contained in a separate indictment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(5) the counts may subsequently be proceeded on as if contained in a separate indictment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 591(6) the accused may be tried separately on the counts as if contained in a separate indictment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 591(6) the accused may be tried separately on the counts as if contained in a separate indictment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 592 to 596`

#ASSERT `s 592 the person may be indicted as an accessory after the fact` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- whether or not the principal has been indicted or convicted or is amenable to justice: none of those facts enters
#ASSERT `s 592 the person may be indicted as an accessory after the fact` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 593(1) any number of persons may be charged in the same indictment with the offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 354, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 593(1) any number of persons may be charged in the same indictment with the offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 355.4, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 593(1) any number of persons may be charged in the same indictment with the offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 356, "(1)(b)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 593(1) any number of persons may be charged in the same indictment with the offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 356, "(1)(a)") EQUALS NOTHING   -- only paragraph 356(1)(b) is named
#ASSERT `s 593(1) any number of persons may be charged in the same indictment with the offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF 355.5, "") EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): args: two or more persons are charged under (1), the person separately committed the offence.
#ASSERT `s 593(2) the person may be convicted` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 593(2) the person may be convicted` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where, pursuant to subsection (1), two or more persons are charged"
#ASSERT `s 593(2) the person may be convicted` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 594 to 596 what the text shows` EQUALS "[Repealed, R.S., 1985, c. 27 (1st Supp.), s. 120]"
